;; The assign-once FIELD-number registry for the minted messages.
;;
;; APPEND-ONLY, AND A PIN IS PERMANENT. An entry here is a wire contract: it
;; survives the field being deleted, precisely so the number can never be
;; handed to a different field later. Deleting a pin frees a number for reuse,
;; which is the one edit that can break a peer that is already deployed.
;;
;; Grown by `protocol-gen reconcile`, never by generating — a generator that
;; could grow its own registry would assign a number as a side effect of being
;; run.
{"pgfix.Heartbeat" {"seq" 1, "sent_at_ns" 2}}
